//
// The on-screen keyboard surface (RFC-0075 Phase 8b; design artifacts: OnScreenKeyboard,
// docked): a chromeless OVERLAY window that windowd docks to the bottom display edge at the
// band height it owns. One opaque TRAY fills the band: the toolbar on top (language chip ·
// candidates · emoji · clipboard · voice · settings · more · close — TASK-0067B), under it
// exactly one body, the keys or the clipboard's cards, which always takes the same height so
// the keyboard never jumps. The key rows are pure DATA (`svc.ime.rows` from the keymaps SSOT,
// reloaded on `KeymapEvent::Changed`) — 180 languages are 180 data tables, never an `if` tree
// here. The globe key cycles the SYSTEM layout (order = platform data); the change
// round-trips through settingsd and comes back as the next KeymapEvent.
//
// The tray is the floating-surface recipe spelled out — `surfaceOverlay` with a `fill` layer
// on top, `shadow3` and the lit top edge, radius xl on the two corners that do not touch the
// screen edge — rather than `.material(overlay)`: inside that material `glassCard` resolves to
// half the `fill`, and the design keeps the keys raw `glassCard`, LIGHTER than the tray in both
// themes. Geometry (4-pt grid, decision Q1): padding 8, gaps 8, a 36 px toolbar; the key rows
// share what is left of the band, five rows of 44 px in today's 312 px band.

Window {
    style: plain,
    level: overlay,
    resizable: false,
}

Page OskPage {
    Stack {
        Stack {
            OskToolbar { }
            if $state.oskPanel == "clipboard" {
                ClipboardCards { }
            } else {
                KeyRows { }
            }
        }
        .grow(1)
        .gap(8)
        .padding(8)
        .bg(fill)
        .corners(xl, xl, 0, 0)
    }
    .bg(surfaceOverlay)
    .corners(xl, xl, 0, 0)
    .shadow(shadow3, edgeHighlight)
}
